    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Place value",
     "md": "In a whole number every digit has a **place value**: units, tens, hundreds, thousands and so on. In 4 305 the digit 4 means 4 thousands, 3 means 3 hundreds, 0 means no tens and 5 means 5 units. A zero keeps the other digits in their right places."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Order of operations (BODMAS)",
     "md": "Work in this order: **B**rackets, **O**rders (powers and roots), **D**ivision and **M**ultiplication (from left to right), then **A**ddition and **S**ubtraction (from left to right). Example: 2 + 3 × 4 = 2 + 12 = 14, not 20."
    },
