    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "HCF and LCM by prime factors",
     "md": "Write each number as a product of primes (use a factor tree). The **HCF** (highest common factor) is the product of the primes common to both, with the **smallest** powers. The **LCM** (lowest common multiple) is the product of all primes, with the **largest** powers."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Saying 1 is a prime number, or that 2 is not prime (2 is the only even prime).\n- Mixing up HCF (a factor, never bigger than the numbers) and LCM (a multiple, never smaller).\n- Stopping a factor tree before every branch ends in a prime."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1: prime factors",
     "statement": "Write 60 as a product of prime numbers.",
     "steps": [
